Diagram 6: SC-GARR Stochastic Control Loop (Itô Calculus)

```
        Real World: Risk Process R(t) follows drift-diffusion:
        =======================================================
        
        dR(t) = μ_R(t) dt + σ_R(t) dW(t)
        
        μ_R = risk growth rate   σ_R = volatility (fat tails)
        
        GARR Observer:
        ==============
        Alert at random time τ_D with probability D(t) = P(τ_D ≤ t | F_t)
        
        Response: latency λ(t)  ->  mitigation activation at τ_D+λ(t)
        
        Safety capacity S(t):   dS = γ·I{t ≥ τ_D+λ} dt
        
        Net exposure: e(t) = R(t) - S(t)
        
        Lyapunov barrier: V(e) = e²
        
        Itô's Lemma:  E[dV] = [2e(μ_R - γ·P(mitigation active)) + σ_R²] dt
        
        Safety condition (E[dV] ≤ 0):
        =============================
        
        D(t) / λ(t)  ≥  μ_R(t) + σ_R(t)
                |           |       |
                |           |       +-- volatility penalty
                |           +-- risk growth rate
                +-- detection / latency ratio
        
        This is SC-GARR.  If satisfied, E[e(t)] remains bounded away from ruin.
```

